## Context

Ticket 0270 recorded the original Dyne design. The current harness review
workflow now warrants reassessing its premises before committing to a PEP
or implementation. See the design reassessment below.

## Task

Evaluate the original choices below against current execution and a concrete
user need. If a separate Dyne object is justified, document the resulting
design and alternatives in a PEP before implementation:

- state is the DAG (`git merge-base --is-ancestor` is the status field;
  no Status header, not even the file path carries state)
- one object = one plain-text file on the source branch
  (`tickets/merges/<branch>.dyne`); merging into main IS the archival act
  (rejected: dedicated refs, shared registry branch, MR-ticket fusion)
- erg's exact three-section grammar; log = one-liners, body = the
  discussion whose opening post is the description (comment #0)
- multi-writer merges via `merge=union` on `tickets/merges/*.dyne`; prose
  append-only by convention; `dyne check` fences the residual hazard
  (rejected: sibling `.log` file, custom merge driver)
- no archive numbering: the merge commit SHA is the permanent name;
  hooks receive `{sha}` (rejected: merge-time serial, safe but unneeded)
- composed on spec and behavior, one codebase two specs (the 0270
  comparison table is the pre-decision record to preserve)
- the composition seam: grammar by convention, references opaque,
  behavior via exec hooks (`.dynerc`)
- the name: dyne, the CGS unit of force -- erg = dyne x cm; standalone
  binary mirroring erg (rejected: git-mr/git mr, bid, darn)
- the seven invariants and the infrastructure-class security posture
  carried over from erg

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Compare a concrete user task with the current no-forge notes workflow;
      document the demonstrated gap or conclude that no Dyne is needed
- [ ] Recommend the smallest remedy with its authority, transport, data-safety,
      concurrency, and cost implications; if Dyne is justified, document its
      settled design, alternatives, and authority model before 0272 proceeds

## Design reassessment (2026-11-04)

Git notes are the review-evidence store, as the author confirmed. The earlier
`tickets/reviews/` proposal is superseded. Read `docs/dyne-review-contract.md`
for the current harness evidence and the remaining decision. The scope above
records the original design candidates; it does not authorize implementation.
Ticket 0271 must first establish a concrete unmet need and decide whether a
separate Dyne object is warranted. Subsequent format and implementation work
is conditional on that decision. This ticket remains open.
